diff --git a/doc/man/tor.1.txt b/doc/man/tor.1.txt
index a865ebd4bb..72f251dc4f 100644
--- a/doc/man/tor.1.txt
+++ b/doc/man/tor.1.txt
@@ -3148,6 +3148,27 @@ The following options are useful only for a exit relay.
     not defined or set to 0, it is controlled by a consensus parameter. If not
     defined in the consensus, the value is 300. (Default: 0)
 
+The following options are useful only for an onion service directory
+(HSDir). Whatever their value, the requests they apply to are counted on the
+MetricsPort.
+
+[[HSDirOneRequestPerCircuit]] **HSDirOneRequestPerCircuit** **0**|**1**|**auto**::
+
+    Close a circuit that makes more than one onion service descriptor fetch
+    or upload. Tor and Arti clients and onion services make each such request
+    on its own circuit. "auto" means use the consensus parameter. If not
+    defined in the consensus, the value is 0. (Default: auto)
+
+[[HSDirRefuseUnknownPrevHop]] **HSDirRefuseUnknownPrevHop** **0**|**1**|**auto**::
+
+    Refuse, with a 503, an onion service descriptor fetch or upload whose
+    previous hop is not a relay in our consensus or for which we have a
+    descriptor: the check RefuseUnknownExits applies to exit streams. A
+    relay that is new in the client's consensus but not yet in ours is also
+    refused, so clients then use another HSDir. "auto" means use the
+    consensus parameter. If not defined in the consensus, the value is 0.
+    (Default: auto)
+
 
 For onion services, mitigations are a work in progress and multiple options
 are currently available.
